WEBVTT

00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:04.230
So you finally show yourself,
you psycho bastard!

00:00:07.650 --> 00:00:08.820
Fire!

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:12.060
Today's supposed to be
everyone's lucky day.

00:00:12.060 --> 00:00:14.360
...But I guess for you...

00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:16.160
it's going to be an unlucky day!

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:27.240
The time is 5:27 AM.

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:31.960
We've apprehended Shimizu Tsuguji for violating article 1
of the magic prohibition law: committing a murder.

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:36.010
...Where did that wind come from...

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:42.050
I will carry my indomitable hope into the dark night

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:42.050
yami no naka no shinjitsu ga hikari kagayaku you ni

00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:48.340
so that it may light a shining fire of truth there

00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:48.340
kagi no nai kibou wo tokihanatou

00:00:58.730 --> 00:01:03.790
I was born bleeding from my hands,

00:00:58.730 --> 00:01:03.790
naze te no hira no kizu wo daite umareochita imi

00:01:03.790 --> 00:01:07.780
and why was I born not a thousand years in the past or the future,

00:01:03.790 --> 00:01:07.780
sennen kako demo mirai demo naku

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:09.090
but in the present?

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:09.090
erabareta ima

00:01:09.090 --> 00:01:13.440
The scales of justice are fragile

00:01:09.090 --> 00:01:13.440
zen'aku hakaru tenbin wa zeijaku

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:18.500
The waning, waxing moon calls to a flower on the earth

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:18.500
michikakeru tsuki ga izanau gisei no chi ni saita

00:01:18.770 --> 00:01:20.400
the color of blood

00:01:18.770 --> 00:01:20.400
chi no iro no hana

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:22.900
I will give all I have

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:22.900
tatta hitotsu kanau nara

00:01:22.900 --> 00:01:25.560
if it means one of my wishes will come true

00:01:22.900 --> 00:01:25.560
subete wo sasageyou

00:01:25.720 --> 00:01:28.870
I have a "post nubila phoebus" kind of personality

00:01:25.720 --> 00:01:28.870
post nubila phoebus kokoro

00:01:28.950 --> 00:01:30.730
which I will show the world

00:01:28.950 --> 00:01:30.730
kaze ni hanatte

00:01:30.730 --> 00:01:33.730
I want to slash apart the curtain of raven black,

00:01:30.730 --> 00:01:33.730
shikkoku no curtain hikichigiri

00:01:33.790 --> 00:01:36.420
and look at a new world

00:01:33.790 --> 00:01:36.420
chigau sora wo mitemitai

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:39.090
My love stabs at the cracks

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:39.090
sabita unmei no hibiware

00:01:39.340 --> 00:01:41.560
of a stagnant fate

00:01:39.340 --> 00:01:41.560
omoi wa nejikonde

00:01:41.560 --> 00:01:44.420
No matter how long the storm lasts,

00:01:41.560 --> 00:01:44.420
donnani arasoi tsuzuketemo

00:01:44.590 --> 00:01:47.030
time itself will not stop breathing

00:01:44.590 --> 00:01:47.030
toki wa kokyuu wo yamenai

00:01:47.290 --> 00:01:49.790
What remains after destruction, rebirth,

00:01:47.290 --> 00:01:49.790
kowashite tsunde kowashite

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:52.260
and further destruction?

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:52.260
nani ga nokoru darou

00:01:52.260 --> 00:01:54.990
I'm sure I can put an end to a thousand nights of doubt

00:01:52.260 --> 00:01:54.990
sou nanajuuokuban no mayoi mo

00:01:54.990 --> 00:01:58.130
and to the system of the world

00:01:54.990 --> 00:01:58.130
sono haichizu wa kakikaerareru

00:01:58.130 --> 00:02:00.800
I'm sure that one day I will find a place where I can shine

00:01:58.130 --> 00:02:00.800
moetsukitemo kagayakeru basho e

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:05.040
even if only ashes will remain

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:05.040
itsuka tadoritsukeru

00:02:07.610 --> 00:02:12.600
Personality Crisis

00:02:07.610 --> 00:02:12.600
Case 4

00:02:08.850 --> 00:02:10.810
Excuse me, Kamakiri.

00:02:10.810 --> 00:02:13.210
I came in early to try
and get some work done,

00:02:13.210 --> 00:02:14.490
so could you not play that music?

00:02:15.450 --> 00:02:16.760
No idol music?

00:02:16.760 --> 00:02:17.570
No, please.

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:19.510
I see.

00:02:19.510 --> 00:02:21.910
I really like it, though.

00:02:22.340 --> 00:02:24.760
You're always here really early.

00:02:24.760 --> 00:02:26.790
...Does the early bird really catch the wor—

00:02:27.220 --> 00:02:31.030
Well, I <i>did manage to
catch you alone today.</i>

00:02:32.020 --> 00:02:33.050
...Right...

00:02:33.050 --> 00:02:35.190
<i>Now, for our next story.</i>

00:02:35.190 --> 00:02:37.890
<i>The suspect in the serial
killings of fifteen wizards,</i>

00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:40.510
<i>Shimizu Tsuguji,
has just been apprehended.</i>

00:02:41.140 --> 00:02:43.730
So they caught the serial killer!

00:02:41.170 --> 00:02:45.290
<i>This case involves the murders of wizards
...beginning three months ago...</i>

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:45.750
Now I can go guy hunting all I want!

00:02:45.750 --> 00:02:49.690
I spent this entire month worried that
he might come after this hot body of mine!

00:02:49.690 --> 00:02:53.950
I was too scared to go out at night!

00:02:54.530 --> 00:02:58.630
Why do you think he
only targeted wizards?

00:02:58.630 --> 00:03:00.450
I mean, he's a Wud himself.

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:05.230
There are times when people come
to hate others that are just like them.

00:03:05.230 --> 00:03:05.870
Huh?

00:03:05.870 --> 00:03:07.370
According to a rumor I heard,

00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:10.670
there's a wizard book
known as "Grimoire 365"

00:03:10.670 --> 00:03:14.150
which mentions a time when
Wuds would fight one another.

00:03:14.150 --> 00:03:18.180
Apparently you can learn the
complete history of Wuds if you read it.

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:20.430
...Grimoire 365...

00:03:20.430 --> 00:03:23.560
And what does that
have to do with this case?

00:03:25.480 --> 00:03:26.600
Don't ask me!

00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:29.150
I don't have the slightest idea!

00:03:29.150 --> 00:03:33.990
I don't even know if the book <i>exists</i>.

00:03:33.990 --> 00:03:35.690
Oh, come on.

00:03:35.690 --> 00:03:38.340
Hotarin seems pretty eager.

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:40.290
I hear she came in at 9 AM today!

00:03:40.290 --> 00:03:44.450
She's really excited because
she's been given her first police case.

00:03:44.450 --> 00:03:47.350
<i>And Hachimitsu's going
to be right on top of her.</i>

00:03:47.350 --> 00:03:48.310
No way!

00:03:48.310 --> 00:03:50.070
Are they getting it on already?

00:03:50.070 --> 00:03:52.170
Oh, Sasorin, curb your enthusiasm.

00:03:52.170 --> 00:03:55.330
She <i>did say she respects
him as a coworker, though.</i>

00:03:55.330 --> 00:03:56.590
What'd I tell ya?

00:03:58.090 --> 00:04:00.490
H-He's so hot!

00:04:00.490 --> 00:04:01.970
Please come in.

00:04:03.650 --> 00:04:04.840
Thank you.

00:04:10.130 --> 00:04:12.300
Do I have something on my face?

00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:13.770
...Oh, no...

00:04:13.770 --> 00:04:15.630
Maybe I just remind you of him?

00:04:15.630 --> 00:04:16.310
Huh?

00:04:16.310 --> 00:04:19.460
I'm actually here to represent
my twin brother, Tsuguji.

00:04:19.460 --> 00:04:19.950
Oh!

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:22.390
I remember seeing him on TV.

00:04:22.390 --> 00:04:23.610
No wonder you look so familiar.

00:04:23.610 --> 00:04:24.930
...But...

00:04:25.770 --> 00:04:28.960
Defending my brother
would be difficult, right?

00:04:29.360 --> 00:04:31.130
I'm aware of that.

00:04:31.130 --> 00:04:33.210
...But Tsuguji...

00:04:33.210 --> 00:04:38.760
Who would've thought that we'd end up defending
the vicious criminal who murdered fifteen wizards?

00:04:38.760 --> 00:04:42.400
Oh? We're willing to
take on any case, you know.

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:44.850
What matters is whether or not
we stand a chance of winning.

00:04:44.850 --> 00:04:47.640
Huh? Are you nervous, Cecilcchi?

00:04:47.640 --> 00:04:49.610
Not really.

00:04:49.610 --> 00:04:52.910
It's just, our client is a cold-blooded
and inhumane murderer.

00:04:52.910 --> 00:04:54.270
...So it's, uh...

00:04:54.270 --> 00:04:56.290
Article 3 of the magic-prohibition law.

00:04:57.400 --> 00:05:01.820
Protecting Wuds' rights
is our job, remember?

00:05:08.480 --> 00:05:11.610
So tell us everything that happened.

00:05:12.920 --> 00:05:14.500
The first one was a woman.

00:05:15.630 --> 00:05:17.450
She was real slender.

00:05:18.100 --> 00:05:22.080
She had just done her nails
too, so I ripped 'em off.

00:05:22.430 --> 00:05:24.930
I hated her eyelashes, though.

00:05:24.930 --> 00:05:27.400
Natural's the best look for eyes, right?

00:05:27.400 --> 00:05:30.180
So I gouged out her eyeballs!

00:05:30.180 --> 00:05:32.550
I even put her in the bathtub!

00:05:32.550 --> 00:05:35.140
But after I cut open her stomach,

00:05:35.140 --> 00:05:38.620
she started to bleed everywhere,
and all her intestines just poured out.

00:05:47.950 --> 00:05:49.430
...Your hair accessories...

00:05:49.430 --> 00:05:50.330
Huh?

00:05:50.330 --> 00:05:51.620
Were they a present from someone?

00:05:51.620 --> 00:05:53.660
Yeah. They're from my dad.

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:55.920
Is there a meaning to them?

00:05:57.170 --> 00:06:00.550
They're apparently protective stones
blessed by my patron saint.

00:06:00.550 --> 00:06:03.150
My, how pretty they are.

00:06:03.720 --> 00:06:05.590
Could you show me up close?

00:06:15.760 --> 00:06:17.060
What's wrong with you?

00:06:17.060 --> 00:06:19.730
You're turning me on, miss!

00:06:28.780 --> 00:06:31.700
There's no way I can
defend that freak!

00:06:31.700 --> 00:06:34.080
F-Freak?

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:38.830
He doesn't regret anything he did
or feel apologetic toward his victims!

00:06:38.830 --> 00:06:41.130
Plus, he's taking this
entire thing as a joke!

00:06:42.250 --> 00:06:45.000
I never even want to see his face again!

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:47.040
Please take me off this case.

00:06:47.040 --> 00:06:48.260
Cecilcchi!

00:06:49.120 --> 00:06:50.810
I know how you feel,

00:06:50.810 --> 00:06:55.190
but it's our job to
defend the accused, Cecil.

00:06:55.190 --> 00:06:56.210
...But...

00:06:56.210 --> 00:06:57.390
...But that guy's a monster—

00:06:57.390 --> 00:07:02.150
So long as you're a professional,
you'll have to face these things.

00:07:04.190 --> 00:07:07.200
If you can't deal with that,

00:07:07.200 --> 00:07:09.170
then turn in your badge and quit.

00:07:09.170 --> 00:07:10.900
A-Ageha!

00:07:11.380 --> 00:07:13.410
She's so mean!

00:07:14.110 --> 00:07:17.550
...I know I got a little emotional...

00:07:17.550 --> 00:07:22.940
But why would Ageha agree to
defend someone like that, anyway?

00:07:22.940 --> 00:07:26.630
I don't want to defend someone
who's killed fifteen people!

00:07:26.630 --> 00:07:28.370
Hey, are you listening?

00:07:28.370 --> 00:07:29.910
I'm listening.

00:07:29.910 --> 00:07:31.180
How about you say something, then?!

00:07:31.180 --> 00:07:33.610
Why would I respond to a whiner?

00:07:33.610 --> 00:07:34.560
Who's whining?!

00:07:34.560 --> 00:07:38.520
Ageha's clearly in the right about this.

00:07:38.910 --> 00:07:40.910
Maybe so,

00:07:40.910 --> 00:07:42.900
but I'm not wrong, either!

00:07:42.900 --> 00:07:45.910
If you're going to keep whining,
then I'll just put away the curry.

00:07:45.910 --> 00:07:46.900
Huh?!

00:07:47.420 --> 00:07:48.910
Ticked off!

00:07:51.280 --> 00:07:53.070
Would you like some coffee?

00:07:53.070 --> 00:07:55.390
Yes, thank you.

00:07:56.400 --> 00:07:58.670
Are you going through
the trial documents?

00:07:58.670 --> 00:08:01.630
No, I'm looking at the petition
I'm submitting to the Court for Magic.

00:08:01.630 --> 00:08:03.300
A petition?

00:08:03.300 --> 00:08:05.140
For a psychiatric evaluation.

00:08:05.920 --> 00:08:09.570
The Wud serial killer, Shimizu Tsuguji,

00:08:09.980 --> 00:08:12.140
has dissociative identity disorder.

00:08:12.140 --> 00:08:15.310
That's what his
younger brother, Rei, said.

00:08:15.310 --> 00:08:18.440
So he has multiple personalities?

00:08:18.960 --> 00:08:19.940
Indeed.

00:08:19.940 --> 00:08:23.190
Oh, so <i>that's why you took on this case.</i>

00:08:23.190 --> 00:08:25.530
I don't accept cases that can't be won.

00:08:26.900 --> 00:08:30.290
They've put me on all sorts of cases!

00:08:30.290 --> 00:08:33.370
And all of the associates there rely on me!

00:08:33.790 --> 00:08:34.650
Really?

00:08:34.650 --> 00:08:36.620
So I'll do my best to
learn as much as I can.

00:08:36.620 --> 00:08:39.790
I'll make sure you get out
before they carry out your sentence.

00:08:41.640 --> 00:08:46.540
The Court for Magic has never
granted anyone a retrial, Cecil.

00:08:46.540 --> 00:08:51.070
I... I know it'll be hard, but I can't save
you if I just sit back and do nothing!

00:08:51.070 --> 00:08:52.540
I'm not going to give up!

00:08:56.580 --> 00:09:00.100
Did something bad happen at work?

00:09:00.100 --> 00:09:02.470
Huh? Wh-Why?

00:09:02.470 --> 00:09:06.180
I can tell when you're
not your usual self, you know.

00:09:09.030 --> 00:09:11.490
Mom has so much more
...to be worried about...

00:09:12.660 --> 00:09:14.390
I'm so pathetic!

00:09:17.390 --> 00:09:19.830
Our petition for a psychiatric
evaluation was granted.

00:09:19.830 --> 00:09:21.190
Really?

00:09:21.190 --> 00:09:22.690
Thank you very much.

00:09:25.820 --> 00:09:28.390
I realize what a difficult case this must be,

00:09:28.390 --> 00:09:30.300
but I hope you can take care of my brother.

00:09:30.300 --> 00:09:32.880
O-Okay.

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:39.390
Well, if possible, we'd like to know more concerning your brother's condition.

00:09:40.540 --> 00:09:44.070
Well, he used to be a very kind sibling.

00:09:44.070 --> 00:09:47.610
We were victims of parental abuse,

00:09:47.610 --> 00:09:50.650
and my brother would always protect me.

00:09:51.010 --> 00:09:52.670
When were were in middle school,

00:09:52.670 --> 00:09:56.550
social services placed us in an orphanage.

00:09:57.160 --> 00:10:01.730
But it was also then that my brother
started showing symptoms of DID.

00:10:01.730 --> 00:10:04.960
An extremely violent personality
was born within his mind.

00:10:06.330 --> 00:10:11.060
As time passed, that side of his
grew more and more predominant.

00:10:11.060 --> 00:10:15.430
To top it all off, he didn't remember
me when he was in that state.

00:10:15.430 --> 00:10:17.800
...Dissociative identity disorder...

00:10:18.120 --> 00:10:22.610
DID is when each personality
has its own memories.

00:10:22.610 --> 00:10:26.600
Basically, one personality won't remember
what another one experiences.

00:10:26.600 --> 00:10:27.790
Yes.

00:10:27.790 --> 00:10:29.610
That sounds just like my brother.

00:10:29.610 --> 00:10:33.350
I hear that people with the condition
are frequently misunderstood.

00:10:33.350 --> 00:10:36.370
Even if the psychiatric
evaluation confirms it,

00:10:36.370 --> 00:10:39.270
...convincing the court could be difficult...

00:10:39.270 --> 00:10:41.410
No. I believe you can do it.

00:10:42.790 --> 00:10:43.870
Goodbye.

00:10:47.560 --> 00:10:49.630
What are you looking for?

00:10:49.980 --> 00:10:52.390
...The girl with the short black hair...

00:10:52.390 --> 00:10:53.960
I haven't seen her around today.

00:10:53.960 --> 00:10:55.200
You mean Moyoyon?

00:10:55.200 --> 00:10:57.670
How would he know who "Moyoyon" is?

00:10:58.010 --> 00:10:59.450
Tentou Moyo.

00:10:59.450 --> 00:11:01.390
She's my paralegal assistant.

00:11:01.700 --> 00:11:04.220
...Tentou Moyo...

00:11:07.960 --> 00:11:10.140
"The girl with the
short black hair", he says.

00:11:10.140 --> 00:11:12.240
I bet he wants to bang Moyoyon.

00:11:12.240 --> 00:11:13.860
Don't be rude!

00:11:14.190 --> 00:11:15.140
Jeez.

00:11:15.140 --> 00:11:17.370
You really ought to go to
some mountain temple

00:11:17.370 --> 00:11:20.490
and cleanse yourself
of all that perversion.

00:11:20.490 --> 00:11:21.610
Hey!

00:11:21.610 --> 00:11:25.000
You'd better watch your mouth
before I start fondling your tits, Cecilcchi!

00:11:35.200 --> 00:11:35.950
Come on!

00:11:56.070 --> 00:11:59.740
Let me go, or I'll kill her too!

00:11:59.740 --> 00:12:00.780
Ageha!

00:12:03.160 --> 00:12:06.870
Back when we lived with our parents,

00:12:07.380 --> 00:12:11.450
there were some rare occasions
when they'd actually be nice to us.

00:12:11.450 --> 00:12:16.380
They'd sing us a lullaby, a line from
which left quite the impression on us.

00:12:16.380 --> 00:12:18.880
Luca... Mahemzushi.

00:12:27.400 --> 00:12:29.610
How do you feel, Tsuguji?

00:12:31.200 --> 00:12:32.150
...I, uh...

00:12:33.220 --> 00:12:34.310
Where am I?

00:12:35.740 --> 00:12:36.900
What's going on?

00:12:39.110 --> 00:12:41.740
Who are you people?

00:12:41.740 --> 00:12:43.320
Seriously?

00:12:41.740 --> 00:12:43.320
Really?

00:12:45.780 --> 00:12:51.770
Now neither the prosecution nor the judge can
claim that Tsuguji was responsible for his actions.

00:12:51.770 --> 00:12:53.650
He'll be sentenced to
life in prison, I guess.

00:12:53.650 --> 00:12:55.610
If they accept his history of illness,

00:12:55.610 --> 00:12:57.550
he'd have to be put into a medical facility.

00:12:58.120 --> 00:13:00.990
His sentence would
most likely be reduced.

00:13:01.840 --> 00:13:04.090
Aren't you hungry, Cecilcchi?

00:13:04.940 --> 00:13:07.810
I have no idea what to think anymore.

00:13:07.810 --> 00:13:08.730
What do you mean?

00:13:08.730 --> 00:13:09.590
...Well...

00:13:09.590 --> 00:13:14.630
I can understand that Tsuguji
may have been a nice person at heart.

00:13:14.630 --> 00:13:20.610
But that doesn't change the fact
that he's killed fifteen people just for fun.

00:13:20.610 --> 00:13:24.010
He may be one in body, but these are
multiple personalities we're talking about.

00:13:24.010 --> 00:13:26.810
Is executing someone for crimes he doesn't
remember committing really justifiable?

00:13:26.810 --> 00:13:27.870
Is that what's on your mind?

00:13:27.870 --> 00:13:29.250
...W-Well...

00:13:29.250 --> 00:13:32.750
I'm wondering whether or not
Tsuguji was a victim himself,

00:13:32.750 --> 00:13:35.670
and what would be the right thing
to do as a wizard barrister.

00:13:35.670 --> 00:13:37.140
Well, that's simple.

00:13:37.140 --> 00:13:40.880
Wizard barristers just have to
put the defendant's interests first.

00:13:40.880 --> 00:13:43.180
Leave your moral compass at home.

00:13:43.180 --> 00:13:46.470
But I can't do that as
easily as you, Natcchi.

00:13:47.600 --> 00:13:50.290
Why did you become a
wizard barrister, then?

00:13:50.290 --> 00:13:54.140
You already knew that we're
seen as villains by the public.

00:13:56.060 --> 00:14:00.050
Well, just relax, you two.

00:14:00.050 --> 00:14:02.570
There's no ready-made
answer for this kinda thing.

00:14:02.570 --> 00:14:05.730
Take your time and come to
your own conclusion, all right?

00:14:05.730 --> 00:14:06.450
Okay.

00:14:06.450 --> 00:14:08.330
You're too naïve.

00:14:08.330 --> 00:14:14.450
The psychiatric evaluation has proved that the
defendant suffers from dissociative identity disorder.

00:14:14.450 --> 00:14:15.330
...Thus...

00:14:16.710 --> 00:14:21.960
the defense believes the defendant
should not be held accountable

00:14:22.400 --> 00:14:24.300
for his actions on the days in question.

00:14:26.900 --> 00:14:28.050
The verdict:

00:14:28.470 --> 00:14:31.430
the defendant is
sentenced to life in prison.

00:14:31.430 --> 00:14:36.610
The results of the defendant's psychiatric
evaluation and the abuse he faced as a child

00:14:36.610 --> 00:14:39.190
provide reasonable grounds for acquittal.

00:14:39.560 --> 00:14:43.990
However, that does not change the fact
that he has killed fifteen wizards.

00:14:43.990 --> 00:14:49.580
Considering the negative effect this case has had on
our society, he will still have to be imprisoned for life.

00:14:49.580 --> 00:14:54.990
That said, the defendant will be given
special permission to stay at a medical facility

00:14:54.990 --> 00:14:57.790
and have his dissociative
identity disorder treated.

00:14:57.790 --> 00:14:59.210
All right!

00:14:59.210 --> 00:15:00.510
That's ridiculous!

00:15:00.510 --> 00:15:02.830
<i>Is this really okay?</i>

00:15:04.340 --> 00:15:06.490
Thank you very much.

00:15:06.490 --> 00:15:07.840
This is all thanks to you.

00:15:07.840 --> 00:15:09.990
No, not at all.

00:15:09.990 --> 00:15:13.390
We hope Tsuguji gets better soon.

00:15:13.990 --> 00:15:14.930
Let's go.

00:15:18.730 --> 00:15:20.900
Those charms seem
to have done the trick.

00:15:20.900 --> 00:15:23.300
Huh? What was that?

00:15:24.480 --> 00:15:28.110
Not only did they protect you, but they also protected <i>me</i>.

00:15:43.890 --> 00:15:47.830
DID is when each personality
has its own memories.

00:15:47.830 --> 00:15:52.010
Basically, one personality won't
remember what another one experiences.

00:15:52.380 --> 00:15:53.510
...And yet...

00:15:53.510 --> 00:15:55.710
<i>he knew about my hair accessories.</i>

00:16:16.620 --> 00:16:18.960
What brings you here so late?

00:16:18.960 --> 00:16:22.350
Your brother's dissociative
...identity disorder...

00:16:24.420 --> 00:16:25.770
...East-southeast...

00:16:25.770 --> 00:16:27.290
...Two fragments...

00:16:27.290 --> 00:16:28.050
...A box...

00:16:28.050 --> 00:16:29.300
...Fresh blood of a maiden...

00:16:29.920 --> 00:16:32.170
Wait, what was that?

00:16:32.170 --> 00:16:33.210
Blood?

00:16:33.920 --> 00:16:34.930
Blood?!

00:16:35.480 --> 00:16:36.910
...East-southeast...

00:16:36.910 --> 00:16:38.750
...Two fragments...

00:16:38.750 --> 00:16:39.350
...A box...

00:16:39.740 --> 00:16:40.970
...Blood...

00:16:40.970 --> 00:16:42.870
It can't be!

00:16:42.870 --> 00:16:43.860
Cecilcchi!

00:16:44.690 --> 00:16:46.430
...The number you have dialed...

00:16:47.120 --> 00:16:48.690
Can I still make it?

00:16:48.690 --> 00:16:49.850
Huh?

00:16:49.850 --> 00:16:51.680
It came up in my divination!

00:16:51.680 --> 00:16:55.070
Something bad's
gonna happen to Cecilcchi!

00:16:55.720 --> 00:16:57.310
Is that true?

00:16:57.310 --> 00:17:00.740
You know that my divinations
are never wrong, Hachimitsu.

00:17:00.740 --> 00:17:02.390
Meet up with Ageha
and get there at once.

00:17:02.390 --> 00:17:04.130
I'll call Inspector Quinn!

00:17:04.800 --> 00:17:05.750
And?

00:17:05.750 --> 00:17:07.550
What makes you say it's a lie?

00:17:08.000 --> 00:17:13.270
The dissociative identity disorder was all
a ruse to have Tsuguji's sentence reduced.

00:17:13.270 --> 00:17:14.640
Am I wrong?

00:17:16.020 --> 00:17:18.100
And what if it was?

00:17:19.470 --> 00:17:23.690
Our objective wasn't to have
Tsuguji's sentence reduced, though.

00:17:24.650 --> 00:17:28.230
It was <i>you</i>, Sudou Cecil.

00:17:29.500 --> 00:17:32.570
So, when is your mother's execution?

00:17:33.570 --> 00:17:38.630
I'm pretty sure the Minister of Justice
will be finalizing the paperwork soon.

00:17:38.630 --> 00:17:40.190
How do you know about that?

00:17:40.190 --> 00:17:44.410
She killed someone in a
bid to protect you, right?

00:17:44.410 --> 00:17:46.630
It could be seen as justifiable homicide,

00:17:46.630 --> 00:17:49.380
but she might've intended
to kill them all along.

00:17:49.380 --> 00:17:51.320
Wh-What are you saying?!

00:17:51.320 --> 00:17:52.340
There's no way!

00:17:52.340 --> 00:17:55.410
Do not request a retrial.

00:17:55.410 --> 00:17:57.130
That's stupid!

00:18:02.210 --> 00:18:04.130
<i>Cecil Diaboloid...</i>

00:18:04.130 --> 00:18:05.470
Go!

00:18:06.120 --> 00:18:08.810
You can't use your diaboloid in here.

00:18:20.270 --> 00:18:22.250
My powers won't stabilize?

00:18:22.250 --> 00:18:27.840
I guess it <i>is true that you have
powers other than your diaboloid.</i>

00:18:27.840 --> 00:18:29.800
Tsuguji was spot-on!

00:18:29.800 --> 00:18:32.210
If you hadn't been a target,

00:18:32.210 --> 00:18:34.970
then we'd have loved to have
added you to our collection.

00:18:34.970 --> 00:18:36.300
Target?

00:18:43.620 --> 00:18:44.810
Hachimitsu?

00:18:45.520 --> 00:18:46.480
Ageha!

00:18:46.480 --> 00:18:47.690
Cecil!

00:18:48.610 --> 00:18:49.650
Stay back!

00:18:50.320 --> 00:18:53.320
...If you don't, then I can't promise her...

00:18:53.880 --> 00:18:54.860
...Her...

00:18:57.320 --> 00:18:58.660
Who are you?!

00:19:05.250 --> 00:19:06.540
Cecil!

00:19:06.540 --> 00:19:07.800
Sudou!

00:19:07.800 --> 00:19:09.000
Cecilun!

00:19:09.380 --> 00:19:11.150
Cecilun, are you okay?

00:19:11.150 --> 00:19:12.590
...S-Somehow...

00:19:16.720 --> 00:19:18.180
A metamoloid?

00:19:18.710 --> 00:19:19.750
...Sasori...

00:19:19.750 --> 00:19:20.800
Quinn! Ekusou!

00:19:32.700 --> 00:19:34.070
How pointless!

00:19:42.870 --> 00:19:44.910
C-Cecil?!

00:19:44.910 --> 00:19:47.000
Is this... sand magic?

00:19:47.000 --> 00:19:49.650
Don't tell me she's having
another awakening.

00:19:49.650 --> 00:19:50.950
Woo-hoo!

00:19:50.950 --> 00:19:52.500
Go, go! Cecilun!

00:19:58.690 --> 00:19:59.720
Take that!

00:20:13.920 --> 00:20:14.970
Wow.

00:20:14.970 --> 00:20:17.450
...Butterfly associates...

00:20:18.700 --> 00:20:20.870
Oh, uh.

00:20:20.870 --> 00:20:22.090
...Well, um...

00:20:22.090 --> 00:20:25.810
I think article 10 of the
magic-prohibition law counts here.

00:20:25.810 --> 00:20:28.330
And I mean, you were able to arrest him.

00:20:30.440 --> 00:20:31.670
Good grief.

00:20:31.670 --> 00:20:33.290
Butterfly Law Offices

00:20:32.340 --> 00:20:36.070
So it seems Tsuguji and Rei
were in on it together.

00:20:36.550 --> 00:20:39.910
It was all an act to get him
off the hook with the law?

00:20:39.910 --> 00:20:43.050
Rotten to the core, both of them!

00:20:43.620 --> 00:20:45.370
Oh, thank you!

00:20:45.370 --> 00:20:46.950
Anyway, how're you doing?

00:20:46.950 --> 00:20:51.070
The case you were handling with
Hachimitsu was drug-related, wasn't it?

00:20:51.070 --> 00:20:52.440
How did it go?

00:20:52.440 --> 00:20:55.440
Well, the defendant regretted his actions.

00:20:55.440 --> 00:20:57.030
Regretted, huh?

00:20:57.030 --> 00:21:00.200
If only those two felt
the same about their crimes.

00:21:00.200 --> 00:21:03.370
Well, you're bound to
get all sorts of cases.

00:21:03.370 --> 00:21:05.430
There are those who are truly evil,

00:21:05.430 --> 00:21:08.670
and those who turn to crime
because they have no choice.

00:21:08.670 --> 00:21:09.750
...Ageha...

00:21:10.210 --> 00:21:15.960
If they asked you to represent
them now, what would you do?

00:21:15.960 --> 00:21:18.210
I'd take on the case.

00:21:18.210 --> 00:21:21.220
Only if there was a
chance of winning, of course.

00:21:23.020 --> 00:21:26.720
I might oppose that again.

00:21:29.660 --> 00:21:31.600
Hey, Moyoyon.

00:21:31.600 --> 00:21:33.130
I didn't even call you.

00:21:33.130 --> 00:21:35.860
How did you know where we were?

00:21:35.860 --> 00:21:38.630
Oh, woman's intuition.

00:21:38.630 --> 00:21:41.860
I can totally sense when
Cecilun is in trouble!

00:21:41.860 --> 00:21:42.990
Right, Cecilun?

00:21:42.990 --> 00:21:45.240
Huh? What?

00:21:46.320 --> 00:21:49.740
It was <i>you</i>, Sudou Cecil.

00:21:51.080 --> 00:21:53.750
I <i>was their objective?</i>

00:22:00.900 --> 00:22:03.260
Was that good enough?

00:22:03.680 --> 00:22:05.110
It was perfect.

00:22:05.110 --> 00:22:08.470
Sudou Cecil's magic
had another awakening.

00:22:26.270 --> 00:22:33.210
My heart may cry silently,

00:22:26.270 --> 00:22:33.210
kokoro ga donna ni namida afuretemo

00:22:33.610 --> 00:22:40.770
but I still want to behold the blue sky

00:22:33.610 --> 00:22:40.770
hitomi ni aozora utsushiteitai

00:22:41.010 --> 00:22:48.340
I want to have something like the strength of flowers

00:22:41.010 --> 00:22:48.340
concrete-iro no machi no katasumi ni

00:22:48.340 --> 00:22:55.740
which bloom in the nooks of the endless concrete of the city

00:22:48.340 --> 00:22:55.740
sotto saku hana no tsuyosa wo manetai

00:22:55.740 --> 00:23:03.170
Starting today, I won't try to wriggle out by saying

00:22:55.740 --> 00:23:03.170
maegami ga jama de mienai nante iiwake

00:23:03.170 --> 00:23:07.010
that I saw nothing because my hair was in the way

00:23:03.170 --> 00:23:07.010
kyou kara shinai

00:23:07.960 --> 00:23:15.450
Beyond the horizon, my future awaits me,

00:23:07.960 --> 00:23:15.450
chiheisen no mukou ni ashita ga matteru kara

00:23:15.450 --> 00:23:20.670
so I will let the sun in my heart

00:23:15.450 --> 00:23:20.670
kono mune no hitotsu no taiyou

00:23:20.670 --> 00:23:22.720
shine out far and wide

00:23:20.670 --> 00:23:22.720
tooku hanatte

00:23:22.720 --> 00:23:30.090
I will overtake the earth's rotation on the path I walk,

00:23:22.720 --> 00:23:30.090
chikyuu no jiten wo oikosu kurai hitamuki ni arukou

00:23:30.090 --> 00:23:38.180
with trusting love inside my heart

00:23:30.090 --> 00:23:38.180
shinjiru omoi dakishimete doko made mo
